# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system config, so a default
# Windows clone materializes every tracked text file with CRLF while the index
# stores LF. Source read through the ES and CSS parsers is normalized on the way
# into the bundle, but esbuild.config.mjs reads CHANGELOG.md as raw text and
# injects it through `define`, so a CRLF checkout ships those bytes inside the
# embedded changelog string and `npm run build:release` on Windows produces a
# main.js that differs from the ubuntu-latest release build at an identical
# commit and toolchain. Pin the working tree to LF for everyone.
#
# A fixture that must carry literal CRLF bytes needs its own `-text` rule below;
# otherwise this line normalizes it away on checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf
